{
    "_notes": "ST LSM9DS1 9-axis IMU, the accelerometer and gyroscope part at 0x6B (SDO_AG high, the Adafruit default) or 0x6A; the magnetometer is a separate I2C device (LSM9DS1M). 8-bit registers\nDetection: WHO_AM_I (0x0F) = 0x68 (LSM6DS3 parts at the same addresses read 0x69 or 0x6A)\nInit: CTRL_REG8 (0x22) = 0x05 - software reset (with IF_ADD_INC), 10 ms; CTRL_REG8 = 0x44 - block data update, address auto-increment; CTRL_REG1_G (0x10) = 0x68 - gyro 119 Hz, +/-500 dps; CTRL_REG6_XL (0x20) = 0x70 - accelerometer 119 Hz, +/-4 g\nPoll (100 ms): OUT_TEMP and the gyro outputs in one read of 8 bytes from 0x15 - the address increments from 0x16 straight to 0x18, leaving out STATUS_REG (0x17), as seen on the bench (a read from 0x17 does include it) - then the accelerometer outputs (0x28-0x2D); all little-endian 16-bit. Gyro 17.5 mdps per count, accelerometer 0.122 mg per count (8192 per g), temperature 16 per degC with 0 at 25 degC.\nSource: registers from the ST LSM9DS1 datasheet",
    "addresses": "0x6a-0x6b",
    "detectionValues": "0x0f=0x68",
    "initValues": "0x2205=p10&0x2244&0x1068&0x2070",
    "pollInfo": {
